-{
-  "slug": "features",
-  "title": "Features",
-  "summary": "What changes from Classic, and what every Nightcap player should know.",
-  "body": "<p class=\"feature-intro\">The major departures from Classic, with the rules you need before your next adventure. Start with a topic below, then follow its guide for requirements and limits.</p><p class=\"notice\">These systems are deployed for live testing. Balance and some gameplay checks remain ongoing. <a href=\"unreleased.html\">In development</a> lists work that is not yet available.</p><h2 id=\"character\">Build one character from three classes</h2><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Three classes from level 1</h3><div><p>Keep your starting class and choose two different extra classes. Your held classes shape spell access, equipment, skills, and base health and mana.</p><a href=\"multiclass.html#three-classes\">Choose your classes →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>AA progression from the beginning</h3><div><p>Allowed AA ranks open at level 1. With focus off, earn full leveling XP plus 20% passive AA experience; full AA focus is also available. Points and prerequisites still matter.</p><a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">Understand AA progression →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Scribe spells ahead of time</h3><div><p>Eligible scrolls can enter your spellbook early. Memorizing and casting still require the normal level for a class you hold.</p><a href=\"multiclass.html#spell-access\">Learn the spell rules →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>A roster of companions</h3><div><p>Multiple summoned pets, selected-pet or All-pets commands, and stored pet armor support a multiclass roster.</p><a href=\"pets.html\">Manage your pets →</a></div></section></div><h2 id=\"rewards\">Earn, trade and upgrade your gear</h2><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Stronger item qualities and zone rewards</h3><div><p>Ordinary tiered gear and the 48-zone reward hunt offer distinct quality families. Hunt augments fit six armor locations and add heroic stats.</p><a href=\"zone-hunt.html\">Explore rewards and sockets →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Turn duplicates into upgrades</h3><div><p>Use three Base zone rewards for Polished, then four matching copies for each higher step. Veyra’s reusable box also upgrades eligible ordinary Polished and Exalted items.</p><a href=\"item-upgrades.html\">See the upgrade recipes →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Free trading and no LORE limit</h3><div><p>Trade formerly restricted and attuned items and keep duplicate LORE items. Inventory space, temporary lifetime and other item rules still apply.</p><a href=\"equipment.html#free-trade\">Read trading and resale rules →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Equipment for your held classes</h3><div><p>Wear ordinary equipment allowed by any held class, regardless of playable race. Other restrictions, including slot, level and deity, remain.</p><a href=\"multiclass.html#equipment-access\">Check equipment eligibility →</a></div></section></div><h2 id=\"adventuring\">Prepare in the tunnel, then explore</h2><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>A shared home base</h3><div><p>New characters start with a kit and 100 platinum in the East Commonlands tunnel. Trainers, spell shops, supplies, banking, buffs and travel services are gathered there.</p><a href=\"tunnel.html\">Meet the tunnel services →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Travel, discovery and private dungeons</h3><div><p>Use tunnel travel services, discover waypoint destinations and enter supported personal dungeon instances. Ancient Attunement recalls you home without changing your bind.</p><a href=\"travel.html\">Plan your journey →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Lasting blessings; temporary combat abilities</h3><div><p>Ordinary beneficial blessings persist on players and owned pets. Temporary AA effects, disciplines and short-duration effects retain their timers.</p><a href=\"combat.html#buffs\">Know which effects last →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Keep fighting while you cast</h3><div><p>Damage-over-time spells cast instantly, and melee autoattacks can continue during casting. Mana costs, reuse, resistance and control effects still matter.</p><a href=\"combat.html#casting\">Read the combat changes →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Less upkeep between adventures</h3><div><p>Food and drink are optional. Normal death retains carried equipment, inventory, money and memorized spell gems; beneficial buffs are lost. Preparation, earned gear and encounter execution still matter.</p><a href=\"combat.html\">Read combat and recovery →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Healing without changing your target</h3><div><p>Ordinary heals cast with an enemy or pet selected heal you. Select a player to heal them; specialized and pet-only spells keep their own rules.</p><a href=\"combat.html#healing\">Check healing targets →</a></div></section></div><h2 id=\"tools\">Spend more time playing</h2><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Stacked materials and Craft All</h3><div><p>Use stacks without manually splitting every ingredient. Repeat a recipe with Craft All while retaining normal recipe requirements, success chances and skill gains.</p><a href=\"tradeskills.html\">Use the crafting controls →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Advanced loot and bulk selling</h3><div><p>Use personal loot queues, loot preferences and group rolls. Sell All keeps bags and casting supplies; bank valuable gear before selling.</p><a href=\"advanced-loot.html\">Learn the loot interface →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>One launcher, current updates</h3><div><p>The normal Nightcap shortcut delivers managed game/interface updates and dated patch summaries. Keep your existing folder and personal settings.</p><a href=\"launcher.html\">Update before playing →</a></div></section></div><h2 id=\"updates\">Keep up with changes</h2><p>Read <a href=\"recent-changes.html\">Recent changes</a> for dated updates. Each release review covers affected guides, commands, item and zone pages, and this Features overview together.</p>",
